<title>AZERBAIJAN: Azeri privatisation vouchers jump after govt pleas.</title>
<headline>Azeri privatisation vouchers jump after govt pleas.</headline>
<byline>Lawrence Sheets</byline>
<dateline>BAKU 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The price of Azerbaijan's new privatisation vouchers rose sharply on Tuesday after government pleas to halt panic selling which had eroded their value.</p>
<p>Street dealers in Baku were offering 450,000 manat ($110), for the packet of four coupons on Tuesday morning, more than double the price two days ago when they were going for only 200,000 manat ($50).</p>
</text>
